Discription:
------------
DeepSpace is a multi-node BBS game (real-time). It can only be ran as a 
DOS door for now.  Since it is a DOS door you can test it out via CLI.

Set Up
------
WB 2 or greater required!

Unarc the files in any directory. In the text directory there is a file
called AlienRaces. This text file can be edited to change the names of
the Aliens in the game. You must have some listed in this text file (MAX 50)
It is set up & ready to go already if you do not want to mess with it.
Also in the sub-directory 'text' there is a text file called sysop.txt.
This file should contain all the names of the players that should have
access to the sysop editors in the game. Only have 1 name per-line & no
trailing spaces. This name should match the name passed to the game.
To enter the Sysop Game Editor hit @ at the mainmenu.
Also to enter the Sysop Planet Editor hit ! at the mainmenu. 
The editors are self explainitory. You shouldn't even really need them.
Maybe if a player hasn't called for along time you could delete em, or maybe
someone just blew up your planet and you want to get even!:)

In the directory you unarced the DeepSpace archive, you will have
GameSetUp
DeepHost
DeepSet
DeepSpace
Text (dir)

First you must run GameSetUp to create everything needed for the game. Use
this program to re-roll the game also. You will be prompted for your
registration #. Just ignore this (unless you have registered the game)

In your startup-sequence you have to run the DeepHost program.
Example:
run WORK:Games/DS/DeepHost <NIL: >NIL:
To stop the Host program just run DeepHost again. It will automatically
notify the other one already running. And if there are any Nodes running 
it will shut them down too.
 
You are ready to go! The program has only been tested on a Excelsior BBS
as of now. If you have ran it on any-other BBS please add a comment on the 
bottom of this file giving directions if anything different in the
setup was required.
Also please let us know!

If you are able to adjust the priority DON'T. Just run DeepSpace at 0.
  
DeepSpace Arguments:
--------------------
Usage:
DeepSpace Name/A/M,T=Time/A/N,Echo/S,D=Delay/N

Name      The users name
            /A - Required
            /M - Multiple strings allowed
T=Time    The time allowed to play
            /A - Required
            /N - numbers
Echo      Echo keypress's
            /S - switch
D=Delay   Fight delay instead of default (20000)
            /N - numbers (1 to 200000000)

An example:  DeepSpace John Doe T=120 Echo D=40000
Name is John Doe, Time allowed 120 minutes, Echo on, Delay set to 40000

NOTE: Name & Time are REQUIRED!

Nodes:
------
20 nodes are able to be ran at the same time. Although this has not been
tested. Who has 20 modems anyways?

REGISTRATION:
-------------
The program is crippled. To get the full blown version you must Register.
The cost is only $20. No extra for nodes ect.. Just 20 bux!

Set Up for Excelsior BBS's  (CNET is prob the same?)
--------------------------

Dos door. For the arguments to pass use "%1" for Alias and you can use
%40 for time left on the bbs or what ever, but a time is required.  
Also pass the echo switch

An example for the DOS ARgs.
"%1" T=%40 echo D=40000

Set Up for 4D BBS's (Versions greater than 2.65)
-----------------------------------------------

Well hopefully it will work.. I tweeked 4D's fifo doors a little so
stdio with raw io will work properly (& DeepSpace). If Dale put it in
it will work properly. Here is an example on how to use it in a menu.

D:F path:Deepspace ^]P3% t=^]P7% echo D=40000

^]P3% = EIC for the Users Name or Alias
^]P7% = EIC for time left on BBS. 

